course: dictionary
lesson: 2132
title: Cooking, a word with three jobs
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: The word cooking can be a noun, a verb, or an adjective. Look at the words around it to see which job it does. In «Mum is cooking dinner», cooking is a verb: it is an action happening now. In «I love Dad's cooking», it is a noun: the food someone makes.
explain: Context helps you choose. «Every cooking machine in the kitchen does one job: it turns electricity or burning gas into heat.» Here cooking is an adjective, because it describes the machine. Ask yourself: what is being done, or what is being described? That tells you the job of the word.
explain: Keep in mind what cooking means: making food ready to eat by heating it, such as baking, boiling or frying. Now try your meaning in the sentence. «A joke feud, like a cooking contest between neighbours, is fine as long as everyone is in on the joke.» A cooking contest is a contest about making food, so the meaning fits.
fact: Cooking means making food ready to eat by heating it, for example by baking, boiling or frying.
fact: «Cooking» can be a noun (the food someone makes), a verb (making food now), or an adjective (describing something, like «cooking oil»).
fact: The -ing form of cook is cooking: cook, cooks, cooked, cooking.
fact: «Natural gas for cooking and heating has no smell of its own, so gas companies add a chemical that smells like rotten eggs, just so people notice a leak.»
fact: Safety first: only cook with an adult, turn pan handles inwards, use oven gloves, and never leave cooking alone.
exercise: «Mum is cooking dinner.» What job does cooking do in this sentence? | An adjective: describing a pan | A noun: the food someone makes | A name for a kitchen | *A verb: making food now
exercise: «I love Dad's cooking.» What does cooking mean here? | A kitchen tool for stirring | Making food now | *The food someone makes | A safety rule for hot oil
exercise: Find the adjective in this sentence: «Every cooking machine in the kitchen does one job.» | one | machine | kitchen | *cooking
test: Which sentence uses cooking as a noun? | *«I love Dad's cooking.» | «Mum is cooking dinner.» | «Cooking apples are sour.»
test: What is the best meaning of cooking? | *Making food ready to eat by heating it | Setting the table for guests | Buying food from a shop | Washing up after a meal
exam: «Natural gas for cooking and heating has no smell of its own, so gas companies add a chemical just so people notice a leak.» What does the chemical smell like? | *Rotten eggs | Burnt toast | Sweet sugar | Fresh flowers
